385	        "Sydney", "NSW", "Melbourne", "VIC", "Brisbane", "QLD");
386	
387	    /** Region -> inclusive 4-digit postcode range {low, high} for the {@code region} derivation. */
388	    private static final Map<String, int[]> REGION_POSTCODES = Map.of(
389	        "NSW", new int[] {2000, 2099}, "VIC", new int[] {3000, 3099}, "QLD", new int[] {4000, 4099});
390	
391	    /** Region -> IANA timezone for the {@code timezone} derivation. */
392	    private static final Map<String, String> REGION_TIMEZONE = Map.of(
393	        "NSW", "Australia/Sydney", "VIC", "Australia/Melbourne", "QLD", "Australia/Brisbane");
394	
395	    /**
396	     * The region code that forms the {@code REGION} segment of the {@link #customerCode}, derived
397	     * by looking up the region by {@link #postcode} range first (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099,
398	     * QLD 4000-4099), and only falling back to the fixed city-to-region table (Sydney->NSW,
399	     * Melbourne->VIC, Brisbane->QLD) when the postcode is absent or in no known range. Returns
400	     * {@code UNKNOWN} when neither source resolves a region.
401	     */
402	    @Transient
